# Orchestration (Guang)

## 1. Context hygiene

After each wave/merge, or when context feels ~60% full:

1. **Persist and push** `.planning/STATE.md`, `.planning/paused/exec-ledger.md`, `HANDOFF.md`, and plan `SUMMARY.md` files.
2. **Compact** working memory: keep only standing rules, current wave, ledger, and next steps — not full transcripts or tool dumps.
3. **Subagents** get a fresh minimal brief: `.planning/paused/p3-common.md` (or phase equivalent) **plus that plan’s PLAN file only**.
4. **Large output** → write to disk; read only what you need; never paste huge logs into chat.

## 2. Parallelism

- Run **exactly 4 concurrent executors** whenever dependency-ready, file-disjoint plans exist (never more than one agent per plan id).
- **Never** more than one executor on the same plan id.
- **Before every spawn:** read `.planning/paused/exec-ledger.md` (plan → agent → status); confirm with `cursor-cloud` list (status `RUNNING`) when the UI count looks wrong.
- **Merge refill (same turn):** On any merge to the integration branch, in **one assistant message** (batch): merge tests → ledger update → **all** missing `Task` spawns to restore **4** `RUNNING` → fast-forward every active `wt/*` worktree from trunk (rebase local WIP if ff fails). Do **not** end a turn with &lt;4 executors unless the ledger records **why** (fewer runnable plans).
- **Visibility:** Executors must `git push -u origin exec/<plan>` after each task commit so parallel work is visible on GitHub; orchestrator reports all four bcIds in every status reply.
- **Retry** only after the previous agent for that plan is confirmed stopped (`IDLE`); log duplicates in the ledger.

## 3. Autonomy

- Do everything you can **without asking Guang**. Guang pre-authorizes approvals the work needs (package installs, plan approvals, GSD checkpoints you can run).
- Only when a **human login** is required (dashboard OAuth, missing secret only the user holds), stop **that item**, give Guang the **exact login link**, and keep working on everything else.
- Hard limits unchanged: no secrets or real customer data in commits; push only to the active integration branch; no PR unless asked.